  ('art-and-music-society-tallaght-campus', 'Art & Music Society (Tallaght Campus)', 'Art & Music Society', 'Arts/Cultural/Languages', 'aka. The Pink Pony Club—If you''re interested in art or music, and interested in performing in front of students, we invite you!', 'aka. The Pink Pony Club—If you''re interested in art or music, and interested in performing in front of students, we invite you!

Welcome to the Arts and Music Society (aka. The Pink Pony Club of TU Dublin)

- WHAT WE''RE ABOUT

A club where musicians and artists alike come together and HAVE A BIT OF FUN after college! ¯(ツ)/¯

Members get access to equipment and practice with us. Additionally, all students are welcome to join our weekly events on Thursdays.

- MAIN THING WITH US

1. We aim to make the TU Dublin Tallaght campus as fun and energetic as it can be, with a place for students to dance, practice, and jam out loud music after class.

2. For students to socialise, interact and have some fun with other students in real life, instead of just wasting their lives on their phones (kinda anti-social media)

- SESSIONS AND EVENTS

DANCE/Practice sessions every Tuesday - at the Sports Hall, Room TC101 (17:00 - 19:00)

A weekly get-together for members. Members can choose to do two things:

JAM SESSION — Practice singing/playing an instrument (Usually used to practice a performance for an upcoming event)

Or

DANCE SESSION — Learning how to dance alongside members (we pick a tutorial on YouTube, and pick a song)

Society Event Every Thursday!

From comedy nights to raves to classic karaoke, we''re doing every event we can budget so that almost every student on campus can really look forward to each week.

Check our Society Calendar for events scheduled—we have some big stuff planned; be sure not miss out on the fun

Our Music Equipment:

• PA speakers

• Mic and Mic Stand

• Mini Mixing Board (can be used to DJ)

• Electric Guitar

• Acoustic Guitar

• Electric keyboard (an old one)

• Bass guitar

• Distortion Pedal

• Loop Station Pedal

Ain''t nobody dance no more at Tallaght! (except us).

Join now :D

"EVERY BAD SITUATION - IS A BLUES SONG WAITING TO HAPPEN" - AMY WINEHOUSE

"MUSIC IS THE STRONGEST FORM OF MAGIC" - MARLIYN MANSON', 'Music', 'coral', '', 'Tallaght', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/AampampMLogo_1758456766_th.jpg', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/IMG-20251016-WA0053_1769552770_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzI0MA==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/artandmusicsocietytallaghtcampus', 'tuartsmusic@gmail.com', '[]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "Winning Best Event Poster in TU Dublin (2024-2025)\n\nWon Best Charity Challenge Event (2024-2025)\n\nWhat do you mean it has nothing to do with art or music? Art... is subjective, man\n\nProviding music annually at TU Dublin Tallaght memorial service"}]'::jsonb, '3240', '2026-10-10T16:06:53Z', '["Culture", "Music"]'::jsonb),
  ('asa-society-city-campus', 'ASA Society (City Campus)', 'ASA Society', 'Academic/Course Related', 'The ASA is the Architectural Students Association. The society is based in the Dublin School of Architecture at Linenhall.', 'The ASA is the Architectural Students Association. The society is based in the Dublin School of Architecture at Linenhall. Originally limited to architecture students, the society is open to anyone in TU Dublin interested in architecture, and has members from the architectural technology course, as well as timber technology students, becoming a college society for the whole school.
We represent the architecture students of TU Dublin, providing lecture series, workshops and social events to better link the various years. We aim to provide people with a broader view of architecture and design in general outside of prescribed college work. This year we hope to continue to provide for our members albeit in different formats.

