Irish language room', 'Globe2', 'coral', '2-3 / 10 / 2026 · Conradh na Gaeilge traenáil na gcumann · (Coiste amháin) · (Committee only)', 'City', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/Clipped_image_20241006_195050_1728404931_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/Clipped_image_20241006_195050_1728405007_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA2OA==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/cumanngaelachcitycampus', 'gaeilge@tudublinsu.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/cumanngaelach_tudublin", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "Bunaithe 2023\n\nEstablished 2023"}, {"title": "Achievements", "body": "Gníomhaí Gaeilge 2023 - Cré umha (bronze)\n\nGníomhaí Gaeilge 2023 - Airgead (silver)\n\nGníomhaí Gaeilge 2023 - Airgead (silver)\n\nGníomhaí Gaeilge 2023 - Airgead (silver)"}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "2-3 / 10 / 2026\n\nConradh na Gaeilge traenáil na gcumann\n\n(Coiste amháin)\n\n(Committee only)"}]'::jsonb, '3068', '2026-10-10T16:06:43Z', '["Culture", "Volunteering"]'::jsonb),
  ('czechoslovak-students-society', 'Czechoslovak Students'' Society', 'Czechoslovak Students'' Society', 'Arts/Cultural/Languages', 'The Czechoslovak Society at TUD unites students interested in Czech and Slovak culture through social events, trips, and celebrations.', 'The Czechoslovak Society at TUD unites students interested in Czech and Slovak culture through social events, trips, and celebrations. Everyone’s welcome to join

Who we are and what we do

The Czechoslovak Society at TUD is a student community that brings together everyone interested in Czech and Slovak culture. Whether you’re from the Czech Republic, Slovakia, or simply curious about our traditions, food, and people, you’re welcome to join us. Our goal is to make Dublin feel a bit more like home — a place to connect, share experiences, and enjoy student life together.

We organise regular events such as pub nights, hikes, game evenings, and film screenings of Czech and Slovak classics, along with seasonal gatherings like Christmas parties or national celebrations. We also plan trips around Ireland and casual meetups that bring students together in a fun, friendly atmosphere.

If you’re studying at TUD and want to explore Central European culture while meeting new people, come join the Czechoslovak Society — everyone’s welcome.

Kto sme a čo robíme

Czechoslovak Society at TUD je študentská komunita, ktorá spája všetkých, ktorí majú záujem o českú a slovenskú kultúru. Nezáleží na tom, či pochádzaš z Česka, Slovenska alebo ťa jednoducho zaujímajú naše tradície, jedlo a ľudia – si u nás vítaný. Naším cieľom je vytvoriť v Dubline miesto, ktoré pôsobí trochu ako domov – priestor na spoznávanie, zdieľanie zážitkov a užívanie si študentského života spolu.

Organizujeme pravidelné podujatia ako pub nights, turistické výlety, herné večery, premietania českých a slovenských filmov či sezónne akcie, napríklad vianočné večierky a oslavy štátnych sviatkov. Okrem toho plánujeme aj výlety po Írsku a neformálne stretnutia, kde si môžeš oddýchnuť a spoznať nových ľudí v uvoľnenej atmosfére.

Ak študuješ na TUD a chceš objavovať stredoeurópsku kultúru spolu so super komunitou študentov, pridaj sa k Czechoslovak Society – dvere sú otvorené pre každého.', 'Globe2', 'coral', '', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/IMG_4342_1759315612_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/bannerczechslovak_1738771452_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzI2Nw==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/czechoslovakstudentssociety', null, '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/czsksocietytud/", "label": "@czsksocietytud"}, {"kind": "linktree", "url": "https://linktr.ee/czsksocietytud", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "Během prvního roku jsme rychle vyrostli v živou komunitu. Uspořádali jsme hospodské večery, túry v Bray a Howth, game night, vánoční promítání české klasiky Pelíšky, ale také větší výlety, například do Belfastu. Nechyběly ani menší house party a samozřejmě společná oslava St. Patrick’s Day v našem česko-slovenském stylu.\n\nDuring our very first year, we quickly grew into a lively community. We organised pub nights, hikes in Bray and Howth, a game night, a Christmas movie evening featuring the Czech classic Pelíšky, as well as bigger trips such as a day in Belfast. We also enjoyed casual house gatherings, and of course celebrated St. Patrick’s Day together in our own Czech-Slovak style.\n\nTeď, když běžíme druhým rokem, stavíme na tomto základu a plánujeme ještě více kulturních akcí, socialů a příležitostí, jak propojit české a slovenské studenty na TUD. Sledujte naši cestu na Instagramu: @czsksocietytud\n\nNow running in our second year, we’re building on this foundation with even more cultural events, socials, and opportunities for Czech and Slovak students at TUD to connect. Follow our journey and see what we’re up to on Instagram: @czsksocietytud"}]'::jsonb, '3267', '2026-10-10T16:06:42Z', '["Culture"]'::jsonb),
  ('dance-society-city-campus', 'Dance Society (City Campus)', 'Dance Society', 'Performing Arts', 'Whether you''re hoping to win gold at a national dance competition or just loosen up after a long day of college, we''re here to provide you…', 'Whether you''re hoping to win gold at a national dance competition or just loosen up after a long day of college, we''re here to provide you with just that!

Join the Beehive!

Hi Everyone!!

This year we are offering weekly classes in Hip-Hop, Contemporary, Heels, Afro and more. You will have the chance to experience additional styles, such as Latin or Irish, in the form of workshops spread throughout the year, and to showcase yourself in annual events, such as in our previous Christmas Show or Allstars! Most importantly, you can connect with like-minded, creative people.

We aim to help our members develop their skills, no matter the level they join us at, and are proud to provide them with a platform to express themselves, as well as opportunities even to hold their own classes.

Follow our social medias for class content, competitions, merchandise drops, and more!!', 'Music', 'plum', 'Weekly Classes & Workshops (open to both Students and NON-Students) · - HipHop · - Commercial · - Dancehall · - Afro Fusion · - Waacking', 'City', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/ProfilePhoto_1-100_1696178907_th.jpg', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/_MG_8650_1602062642_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA2OQ==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/dancesocietycitycampus', 'dance@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublincc_dance_soc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "tiktok", "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@tudublinccdancesoc", "label": null}, {"kind": "facebook", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/TUDublinCCdancesoc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "x", "url": "https://x.com/TUDublinCCDance", "label": null}, {"kind": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/@tudublindancesociety5557", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "Our Dance Society was established during the days of DIT (DIT Dance Soc) and through the hard work and passion of our alumni committees members and dancers it has now evolved into the amazing, strong and energetic TUD Dance Soc full of hardworking-talented dancers.\n\nLike our predecessors, we hope to continue to foster a community for students with interests in all areas of dance and performing art, and celebrate the cultures and stories behind each dance-style, and celebrate the creativity and talents of all of the students who are part of our community here in TU Dublin Dance Society!"}, {"title": "Achievements", "body": "TU Dublin City Campus'' Best Society Overall\n- 2017\n- 2018\n- 2020\n\nTUD''s Most Active Society\n- 2023\n- 2026\n\nIrish Intervarsity Hip-hop Champions\n- 2018\n\n- 2019\n\n- 2020\n\n- 2023\n\n- 2024\n\n- 2025\n\n- 2026\n\nIrish Intervarsity Mixed Piece Champions\n\n- 2025\n\n- 2026"}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "Weekly Classes & Workshops (open to both Students and NON-Students)\n\n- HipHop\n\n- Commercial\n\n- Dancehall\n\n- Afro Fusion\n\n- Waacking\n\n- Kpop\n\n- Locking\n\n... and many more!\n\nCrew Trainings\n\nSocial Events\n\n- Pub Quizzes\n\n- Bingo Night\n\n- All Stars\n\n... More to come"}]'::jsonb, '3069', '2026-10-10T16:06:40Z', '["Arts", "Music"]'::jsonb),
  ('disney-society', 'Disney Society', 'Disney Society', 'Special Interest/Social', 'The Disney Society is a great place to make friends, watch Disney, Pixar, Marvel and Barbie movies and do arts and crafts and much more.', 'The Disney Society is a great place to make friends, watch Disney, Pixar, Marvel and Barbie movies and do arts and crafts and much more.
The Disney Society is a great place to make friends, watch Disney, Pixar, Marvel and Barbie movies and do arts and crafts and Much more.

Follow our Instagram @Tud_Disney_Society for more information and updates ✨️', 'Clapperboard', 'emerald', '', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/download_1668538311_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/Disney-background_1668535885_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzIzNg==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/disneysociety', 'disney@socs.dit.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tud_disney_society", "label": null}, {"kind": "discord", "url": "https://discord.gg/rBe8rVK7", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '3236', '2026-10-10T16:06:39Z', '["Arts"]'::jsonb),
  ('dj-society-city-campus', 'DJ Society (City Campus)', 'DJ Society', 'Special Interest/Social', 'Since the 2010s, we’ve been a hub for DJs of all levels, offering lessons and Freemix sessions, our members regularly book gigs and excel…', 'Since the 2010s, we’ve been a hub for DJs of all levels, offering lessons and Freemix sessions, our members regularly book gigs and excel in the music scene. With great gear, inclusive events, and a supportive community, we’re here to help you grow.
Since the 2010s, the DJ Society has been a cornerstone of Ireland’s student music scene, bringing together aspiring and experienced DJs to share their passion for music. We’re a community built on creativity, collaboration, and a love for the art of DJing. Whether you’re just starting out or already spinning tracks, there’s a place for you here.

Every Monday, we host lessons tailored to all skill levels, from beginners learning the basics to advanced DJs refining their techniques. Fridays are reserved for our Freemix sessions, where members take to the decks to showcase their skills, experiment with new sounds, and enjoy the energy of a live audience. It’s the perfect space to grow, connect, and express yourself through music.

We’re also committed to fostering inclusivity and representation within the music world. Our annual Women’s Day event, featuring an all-women lineup, is a celebration of the incredible contributions of women in the industry and a platform to inspire the next generation of female DJs. With access to high-quality equipment and a supportive, tight-knit community, the DJ Society is more than just a society—it’s a launchpad for growth, creativity, and success.

Join us and be part of a community that’s all about music, connection, and making waves.', 'Music', 'emerald', 'DJ Lessons · Day · Time · Level · Location · Monday · 6pm-9pm · Beginner & Advanced · Aungier St Black Box · DJ Free Mixing · Day · Time', 'City', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/image4_1601842358_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/ScreenShot2023-09-27at15.39.29_1695825581_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA3MQ==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/djsocietycitycampus', 'dj@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublindjsoc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "tiktok", "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@tudublindjsoc", "label": null}, {"kind": "facebook", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/ditdj/", "label": null}, {"kind": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/@tudublindjsoc", "label": null}, {"kind": "whatsapp", "url": "https://chat.whatsapp.com/LodQmPcNMz08wnWWILw7L3", "label": null}, {"kind": "other", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/tuddjsoc", "label": "soundcloud.com"}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "Our achievements are a testament to the talent, hard work, and passion that define the DJ Society. We’ve proudly won the Spinoff National Student DJ Competition twice—in 2018 and again in 2024—showcasing our ability to compete at the highest level. In 2018, we also took home the title for the BICS Best Intervarsity Event, a recognition of our commitment to creating unforgettable experiences. Beyond competitions, our members are making waves in the music industry, regularly booking gigs at clubs, festivals, and private events. Their success is a reflection of the skills and confidence they’ve built here, proving that the DJ Society is a launchpad for real-world achievement.\n\nWe’re also proud of our efforts to promote inclusivity and representation. Our annual Women’s Day event, featuring an all-women lineup, celebrates the incredible contributions of women in the music industry and inspires the next generation of female DJs. These achievements, both on and off the stage, highlight what makes our society special: a community that’s not just about winning, but about growing, connecting, and making a lasting impact."}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "DJ Lessons\n\nDay\n\nTime\n\nLevel\n\nLocation\n\nMonday\n\n6pm-9pm\n\nBeginner & Advanced\n\nAungier St Black Box\n\nDJ Free Mixing\n\nDay\n\nTime\n\nLocation\n\nMonday\n\n6pm-9pm\n\nAungier St Radio Room\n\nFriday\n\n5pm-8pm\n\nAungier St Black Box & Aungier St Radio Room"}]'::jsonb, '3071', '2026-10-10T16:06:38Z', '["Music"]'::jsonb),
  ('drama-society', 'Drama Society', 'Drama Society', 'Performing Arts', 'Interested in drama and theatre, and having the craic? Then Drama Soc is for you!', 'Interested in drama and theatre, and having the craic? Then Drama Soc is for you!
Whether you''re interested in performing, directing, writing, tech/backstage - we''ve got something for everyone!
Interested in drama and theatre, and having the craic? Then Drama Soc is for you!

Whether you''re interested in performing, directing, writing, tech/backstage - we''ve got something for everyone! Even if you just want to make some friends in a relaxed, fun environment. Don''t worry if you have no experience - its not necessary at all! We hold weekly workshops on drama/acting technique as well as other areas of theatre (this will be slightly different this semester, but we have some great ideas for online events!)

We hold a couple of big events throughout the year where our members get to show off their skills - mainly the One-Act Festival in the first semester which consists of several short plays (no audition necessary - just a chance for everyone to have a go!) and the Drama Festival in the second semester which normally features a couple of full length productions.', 'Clapperboard', 'plum', 'Weekly Workshops', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/70949585_2874290892600464_3113889970075467776_n_1601660259_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/20afad32-2bda-4005-9ef7-8d6cb2156d10_1710209083_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA3NA==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/dramasociety', 'drama@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublindramasoc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "facebook", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/TUDublinDramaSoc/", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "Most Improved Society 2020 at BICS"}]'::jsonb, '3074', '2026-10-10T16:06:36Z', '["Arts"]'::jsonb),
  ('eastern-european-society-blanchardstown', 'Eastern European Society (Blanchardstown Campus)', 'Eastern European Society', 'Arts/Cultural/Languages', 'A home away from home for Eastern Europeans and others interested in the culture!', 'A home away from home for Eastern Europeans and others interested in the culture!
As a recently established society, our main objective is to create unity among the diverse cultures and individuals from Eastern Europe in TU Dublin.

We''re really looking forward to this year''s society, and we''ve got lots of interesting activities lined up. You can catch a glimpse of our previous outings and events on our Instagram page @Tudublin_eastern_european_soc. See you there!', 'Globe2', 'coral', '', 'Blanchardstown', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/ees_1695657361_th.jpg', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/278384127_397090252274989_6252814581361928212_n_1698976031_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzIyNg==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/easterneuropeansocietyblanchardstowncampus', 'easterneuropeanbc@socs.dit.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublin_eastern_european_soc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "discord", "url": "https://discord.gg/7bQGmZKyRs", "label": null}, {"kind": "whatsapp", "url": "https://chat.whatsapp.com/BVuQImqsoImA6vJAXRBtdg", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "Winner of Best New Society 2023\n\nWinner of Society Person of the Year: Diana Novak 2023\n\nWinner of Best Society Promotional Video 2023\n\nWinner of Best New Society 2022\n\nWinner of Best Green Initiative 2022\n\nWinner of Best Individual: Diana Novak 2022"}]'::jsonb, '3226', '2026-10-10T16:06:35Z', '["Culture"]'::jsonb),
  ('enactus-society-city-campus', 'Enactus Society (City Campus)', 'Enactus Society', 'Business/Enterprise', 'Enactus is a global social enterprise community of students, academic and business leaders with the sole purpose of encouraging…', 'Enactus is a global social enterprise community of students, academic and business leaders with the sole purpose of encouraging entrepreneurial action to make the world a better place for everyone.
Enactus TU Dublin will give you the opportunity to innovate and experiment with setting up your own business idea or let you take part in projects that are already on their way to becoming successful and sustainable business models. It will give students the perfect opportunity to collaborate with their peers within the university and get the opportunity to work closely with business people who represent their companies who are partnered with Enactus.

Enactus is a global social enterprise community of students, academic and business leaders with the sole purpose of encouraging entrepreneurial action to make the world a better place for everyone.', 'Rocket', 'amber', 'Project Team meetings · Bi-weekly Progress update meetings · Pitching Competitions · Workshops (Conferences, Entrepreneurs/Business Talks)', 'City', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/download_1664114062_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/IMG_7462_1758097432_th.jpeg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzE3NA==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/enactussocietycitycampus', 'enactus@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/enactustudublin/", "label": null}, {"kind": "facebook", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/EnactusTUDublin/", "label": null}, {"kind": "x", "url": "https://twitter.com/enactustudublin", "label": null}, {"kind": "other", "url": "https://enactusuki.or/", "label": "enactusuki.or"}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "Enactus TU Dublin has achieved national and university-wide recognition for our impact-driven projects. In the past year, we were awarded Best New Venture at the TU Dublin Volunteering Awards, Best Charity Event at the TU Dublin Society Awards, and the prestigious National Best Charity Event at the BICS Ireland Awards. Our projects — S’port for Grief, EcoSortX, ReFridge, and ReRetro — continue to grow, showcasing creativity, sustainability, and social innovation. These achievements highlight our society’s commitment to empowering students to drive meaningful change and represent TU Dublin with pride on both a national and community stage."}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "• Project Team meetings\n\n• Bi-weekly Progress update meetings\n\n• Pitching Competitions\n\n• Workshops (Conferences, Entrepreneurs/Business Talks)"}]'::jsonb, '3174', '2026-10-10T16:06:33Z', '["Business", "Volunteering"]'::jsonb),
  ('engineering-society-city-campus', 'Engineering Society (City Campus)', 'Engineering Society', 'Academic/Course Related', 'Are you tired of being the only one in your friend group who geeks out over all things engineering?', 'Are you tired of being the only one in your friend group who geeks out over all things engineering? Do you crave a community of like-minded individuals who share your passion for F1, rockets, and really cool gadgets? Or, do you just fancy going out for a few? Look no further than the engineering society!

We''re a group of engineering enthusiasts who love to build things, break things, and then build them again (hopefully better the second time around). We''re always up for a challenge, whether it''s designing an actually decent McLaren F1 car, launching a rocket, or creating the world''s most complicated Rube Goldberg machine.

Whether you''re a seasoned pro or just starting to explore the world of engineering, we welcome you with open arms (and possibly some awkward dance moves). So come on down and join the fun we promise, we won''t judge you if you still think pi is a dessert

Our society also has an affiliation with engineers Ireland.', 'Cog', 'sky', 'Competitions · Social Events · Trips (F1)', 'City', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/EngSoclogo_1679420744_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/EngineeringSociety1_1679420461_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA3Nw==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/engineeringsocietycitycampus', 'engineering@socs.dit.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublinengsoc/", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "Achievements", "body": "2022 BIC''s Best Departmental Runner-up"}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "Competitions\n\nSocial Events\n\nTrips (F1)"}]'::jsonb, '3077', '2026-10-10T16:06:32Z', '["Science", "Technology"]'::jsonb),
  ('environment-planning-and-sustainability', 'Environment, Planning and Sustainability Society', 'Environment, Planning and…', 'Academic/Course Related', 'The EPS society is a meeting place for those interested in cities, planning and the environment.', 'The EPS society is a meeting place for those interested in cities, planning and the environment. We primarily organise speakers on these topics. We also organise social events for people who are interested in these topics to meet like minded people. We are passionate about creating better places and saving the world. Join us if you are too!
The Environment, Planning and Sustainability society organises social events for its members and guest speakers and lectures on topics of interest to its members. If you are interested in cities, sustainability, town planning and our environment, you will fit right in. We mostly organise our guest lecture events at two big occasions in the year, Green Week in March and Planning Week in November. Our social events can happen anytime members are interested. Examples of some of the speakers we have had:

Audrey Crowe, Limerick City and County Council

Owen Keegan, Dublin City Council CEO

Damien English TD, Minister of State for Housing and Urban Renewal (at the time)

Ronan Lyons from TCD, leading national expert in housing and urban economics

Collie Ennis, researcher in Zoology at TCD

Mark Teevan, Toyota and Hydrogen Mobility Ireland

Brendan O'' Brien, Head of Technical Services at the Environment and Transportation Department, Dublin City Council

Kevin Baker, Dublin Cycling Campaign

Marcello Corsi, Head of Track Design at Transport Infrastructure Ireland', 'Leaf', 'sky', 'Speakers and social events', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/EPSLogoNoBackgroundSq_1665610853_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/Cover_1663070273_th.jpg', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA3OA==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/environment,planningandsustainabilitysociety', 'eps@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/tudublineps/", "label": null}, {"kind": "linktree", "url": "https://linktr.ee/tudublineps", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "The first planning society was called \"DIT Mental Planners.\" They were last active around 2011. The society died off around that time as the numbers doing the BSc in Spatial Planning and Environmental Management died down too during the recession. Our society was started formally in March 2019 with our first events during TU Dublin Green Week. DIT Green Week was started by our school and we are proud to continue the tradition of flying the green week flag under the logo of our new society and our new university. We are still passionately organising events, getting interesting speakers to discuss solutions to our environmental and planning issues which are heavily interlinked."}, {"title": "Achievements", "body": "We were once referred to by current Dublin City Council Chief Executive Officer Owen Keegan as \"A group of sophisticated fuckers!\""}]'::jsonb, '3078', '2026-10-10T16:06:31Z', '["Volunteering", "Outdoors"]'::jsonb),
  ('erasmus-student-network-tu-dublin', 'Erasmus Student Network TU Dublin', 'Erasmus Student Network', 'Special Interest/Social', 'TU Dublin''s society for all exchange/ International/ Irish students', 'TU Dublin''s society for all exchange/ International/ Irish students
Ready to join some of the Erasmus Student Network TU Dublin''s events ?

Follow us on social media to find out more or join our WhatsApp chat via email.

We are also selling ESNcards, please fill out the form in our Linktree to pre-order one.', 'Globe2', 'emerald', '', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/ESNTUDublin_1696941288_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/ESN-TU-Dublin-Cover-Facebook_1683991983_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzA5MQ==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/erasmusstudentnetworktudublin', 'esn@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/esntudublin/", "label": null}, {"kind": "tiktok", "url": "https://www.tiktok.com/@esntudublin", "label": null}, {"kind": "facebook", "url": "https://www.facebook.com/ESNTUDublin", "label": null}, {"kind": "linktree", "url": "https://linktr.ee/esntudublin", "label": null}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "ESN TU Dublin is a local section (society) of the Erasmus Student Network, a not for profit, student-run organisation. ESN works with International, Exchange and Erasmus+ students all over the world and fosters opportunities for intercultural understanding and self-development.\n\nWorking under the principle of “Students helping Students”, ESN TU Dublin is dedicated to helping students of TUD feel at home during their study abroad period through fun events, cultural exchanges, trips and more!\n\nWe also provide support for local students who:\n\nAre getting ready for their upcoming Erasmus/study abroad period.\n\nStudents who are settling back in after finishing their Erasmus/study abroad period.\n\nSo whether you’re looking to make new friends, get support or extend the feeling of your study abroad experience, ESN TUD is the place for you! Become a member today, Erasmus isn''t just one year in your life, it''s a way of life!"}]'::jsonb, '3091', '2026-10-10T16:06:29Z', '["Culture"]'::jsonb),
  ('esports-society', 'Esports Society', 'Esports Society', 'Gaming/Technology', 'Representing TUD in Valorant, League of Legends, Rocket League, Smash and more. Check us out!', 'Representing TUD in Valorant, League of Legends, Rocket League, Smash and more. Check us out!
Whether you''re intensely competitive or just want to meet people and have some fun, we have something for you! We run our own events regularly as well as taking part in national and international competition. TU Dublin is THE top esports institution in Ireland and we''re proud to continue that tradition!

• All skill levels welcome! Including casual gamers who just want to get involved!

• Join solo or with friends!

• We make teams so that everyone gets to play!

• Weekly matches in all our major games!

Games We Play

Each week our teams compete in Irish Esports Collegiate and NUEL run tournaments where they go up against other colleges. We also run a weekly in-person smash tournament. We''re open to running any game if there''s enough interest!

Within TUD:

• Smash Ultimate

Through Ireland Esports Collegiate:

• League of Legends

• VALORANT

• Rocket League

• Counter Strike 2

• Teamfight Tactics

• Rainbow 6 Siege

• Overwatch

Through NUEL and IEC (UK & Ireland):

• League of Legends

• Valorant (Women and Non-Binary tournament available*)

*A full TUD team is not needed to play in the Women and Non-Binary tournaments. They create teams for individuals.

Achievements:

Spring 2023 Results:

GamerFest Collegiate Challenge (Rocket League and Valorant) - 1st Place

Nativz Valorant - 1st Place

Nativz League of Legends - 2nd Place

Nativz Rocket League - 2nd Place

Nativz Formula 1 2022 - 2nd Place

NUEL Rainbow Six Siege- 3rd Place

Winter 2022 Results:

Nativz League of Legends - 1st Place

Nativz Rocket League - 2nd Place

Number #1 Overall in Irish Collegiate Esports since 2022', 'Gamepad2', 'indigo', '', null, 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/TUD-Apes_2_1696769199_th.jpg', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/nativz_leaderboard_2022_2023_cropped_1696896540_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzE3Mg==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/esportssociety', 'esport@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/TUDublinEsports", "label": null}, {"kind": "x", "url": "https://x.com/TUDublinEsports", "label": null}, {"kind": "discord", "url": "https://discord.gg/SefM2GhWSb", "label": null}, {"kind": "linktree", "url": "https://linktr.ee/tudublinesports", "label": null}, {"kind": "other", "url": "https://irelandcollegiate.com/", "label": "Ireland Esports Collegiate"}, {"kind": "other", "url": "https://thenuel.com/", "label": "NUEL"}, {"kind": "other", "url": "https://discord.tudublinesports.ie/", "label": "discord.tudublinesports.ie"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '3172', '2026-10-10T16:06:28Z', '["Gaming"]'::jsonb),
  ('ethical-hackers-society-blanchardstown', 'Ethical Hackers Society (Blanchardstown Campus)', 'Ethical Hackers Society', 'Gaming/Technology', 'Enabling students to be successful in their studies and security through teaching Hacking, CTFs and Networking.', 'Enabling students to be successful in their studies and security through teaching Hacking, CTFs and Networking.

The TU Dublin Ethical Hacker Society is about the teaching of all things regarding security. From physical lock picking to advanced cybersecurity tools. We all teach how to protect yourself against dangerous malware and scams. We host Capture the flag(CTF) events and social nights for our members.', 'Code2', 'indigo', 'Workshops · Gaming · Guest Speakers · Classes', 'Blanchardstown', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/android-chrome-512x512_1733823656_th.png', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/admin/uploads/images/organisation/profile/oldbanner_1733823715_th.png', 'https://mystudentlife.tudublin.ie/account/index.php?object=VXNlck9yZ2FuaXNhdGlvbk1lbWJlcg==&method=Zm9ybVZpZXc=&action=Nw==&systemClientID=Mg==&organisationID=MzE3OQ==&actionType=YWRk', 'https://societies.tudublin.ie/societies/ethicalhackerssocietyblanchardstowncampus', 'ethicalhackers@societies.tudublin.ie', '[{"kind": "instagram", "url": "https://www.instagram.com/hackersoc/", "label": null}, {"kind": "linkedin", "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/groups/8682497/", "label": null}, {"kind": "x", "url": "https://twitter.com/HackerSoc", "label": null}, {"kind": "discord", "url": "https://discord.gg/H8jTgKc3Xe", "label": null}, {"kind": "other", "url": "http://www.hackersoc.com/", "label": "hackersoc.com"}]'::jsonb, '[{"title": "History", "body": "Ethical Hacker Society is a society of Technological University of Dublin (or better known as TU Dublin). Our goal is to offer support in all topics cyber security related and prepare our members to become a part of the future in the cyber security sector.\n\nOriginally founded in 2011 in the Institute of Technology Blanchardstown by alumni and lecturers Hacker Society TU Dublin is now home to 117 active members (in 2023). To this day we still work closely with those lecturers while past pupils host periodic talks on our Discord server."}, {"title": "Achievements", "body": "Along with our frequent social events, we also host a variety of workshops and talks. One central aspect of Hacker Society is the topic of Capture the Flag events (CTFs). We like to encourage participation in CTFs through workshops, talks, and alerting members of any CTF related news. We regularly send out members to international cyber competitions such as the European Cyber Security Challenge (ECSC).\n\nOur members range from completely new to cybersecurity to the more experienced with members who have competed in the European Cyber Security Challenge (ECSC) and won. Although it may seem daunting as a newcomer, everyone must start from somewhere so you’re definitely not alone.\n\nFurthermore, many of our members come from computing and cyber security courses within TU Dublin but all are welcome from across all the courses, enthusiasm and motivation will get you far.\n\nThe need for cyber security is ever growing with no sign of slowing down anytime soon. We hope to support you on your own journey in cyber security."}, {"title": "Meetings", "body": "Workshops\n\nGaming\n\nGuest Speakers\n\nClasses"}]'::jsonb, '3179', '2026-10-10T16:06:27Z', '["Technology"]'::jsonb),
