y": "Gaming Nights\n\nPokémon GO Community Days\n\nDungeons and Dragons campaigns\n\nMovie Nights\n\nChristmas Monopoly\n\nCardboard Events\n\nWarhammer Sessions\n\nCollaborations\n\nTrivia Nights\n\nSocial Nights"}]'::jsonb, '3192', '2026-10-10T16:06:02Z', '["Gaming"]'::jsonb),
  ('neurodivergent-society-tallaght-campus', 'Neurodivergent Society (Tallaght Campus)', 'Neurodivergent Society', 'Special Interest/Social', 'A safe space for people in TU Dublin who are neurodivergent (or identify as such) to commune and socialise.', 'A safe space for people in TU Dublin who are neurodivergent (or identify as such) to commune and socialise.

The Neurodivergent Society at TU Dublin is a vibrant and inclusive community dedicated to supporting neurodivergent students, fostering understanding, and promoting mental well-being. Our mission is to create a safe and welcoming environment where individuals can connect, share experiences, and celebrate the diverse ways of thinking and being.

Sensory Sessions are a key highlight of our events calendar. These gatherings provide a calming space for members to engage in sensory-friendly activities that cater to various needs. From gentle music and soothing lights to tactile play with materials like sand and water beads, these sessions aim to reduce stress and promote relaxation. Participants often find comfort in the shared experience, allowing for open conversations and the development of friendships in a supportive atmosphere.

LEGO Building Days offer a unique blend of creativity and collaboration. Participants can unleash their imagination while working with LEGO bricks to build anything from intricate models to fantastical creations. These sessions encourage teamwork and provide a fun outlet for self-expression. Whether you’re a seasoned builder or a beginner, everyone is welcome to join in the fun and enjoy the therapeutic benefits of hands-on play.

Our Arts and Crafts events are another favorite among members, where creativity knows no bounds. These sessions include a variety of activities, such as painting, drawing, and crafting with different materials. Guided by talented facilitators, participants can explore their artistic side while socializing and sharing ideas. The focus is on process over product, allowing everyone to engage at their own pace and express their individuality.

