  ('tu-dublin-svp-society', 'TU Dublin SVP Society', 'SVP Society', 'Volunteering/Civic/Charity', 'If you''re interested in helping out in the local community and giving back to others, then you''re in the right place.', 'If you''re interested in helping out in the local community and giving back to others, then you''re in the right place.

Welcome to SVP Society (St. Vincent de Paul) at TU Dublin!

A Path to Meaningful Volunteering

First and foremost, SVP Society is your start to meaningful volunteer work that goes beyond just ticking a box. It''s a chance to make a genuine difference in the lives of others while enriching your own college experience. You''ll discover that volunteering during your college years is not just about giving back; it''s also an avenue to forge lasting friendships, explore social justice issues, and have a different kind of fun that leaves a lasting impact.

A Global Community

By joining SVP Society, you''re becoming a part of something much bigger. Our society is part of Colleges SVP, an international organization with over 11,000 dedicated volunteers. This makes us the largest society of our kind in Ireland. However, it''s not just about numbers; it''s about the unique values that drive us forward.

The Pillars of SVP

At SVP Society, we uphold three core pillars that define our mission:

Support & Friendship

Establishing relationships built on trust & friendship through respecting the dignity of those we assist and fostering self-respect.

Promoting Self-Sufficiency

It is not enough to provide short-term material support. Those we assist are also helped to achieve self-sufficiency in the long term.

Working for Social Justice

We are committed to identifying the root causes of poverty and social exclusion, and in solidarity with people experiencing poverty and disadvantage, to advocate and work for the changes required to create a more just and caring society.

Your Journey with Us

